{"id":"zip-0325","number":325,"title":"Account Metadata Keys","status":"Draft","statusDetail":null,"category":"Standards / Wallet","owners":["Jack Grigg","Daira-Emma Hopwood","Kris Nuttycombe"],"created":"2025-02-18","license":"MIT","discussionsTo":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/issues/1233","pullRequest":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/pull/979","kind":"zip","format":"md","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/main/zips/zip-0325.md","official":"https://zips.z.cash/zip-0325","updatedAt":"2026-03-24T14:21:51Z","summary":"This ZIP specifies the key tree for Account Metadata Keys. These are derived from the same seed as a ZIP 32 2 account, and can be used by wallets to derive encryption keys for local / off-chain metadata.","words":1131,"digest":"28b2fa9c137192793811b211a67532542a597a51e00310cc2c3a5460a95a36d1","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"metadatakeytree","title":"Metadata key tree","level":3},{"id":"accountmetadatakey","title":"Account Metadata Key","level":4},{"id":"inherentmetadatakeys","title":"Inherent metadata keys","level":4},{"id":"externalmetadatakeys","title":"External metadata keys","level":4},{"id":"standardisedmetadataprotocols","title":"Standardised metadata protocols","level":3},{"id":"private-usemetadatakeys","title":"Private-use metadata keys","level":3},{"id":"referenceimplementation","title":"Reference implementation","level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key words \"MUST NOT\", \"SHOULD\", and \"MAY\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"href":"#fn:BCP14"}],"id":"fnref:BCP14"}," when, and only when, they appear in all capitals."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP specifies the key tree for Account Metadata Keys. These are derived from the same seed as a ZIP 32 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"href":"#fn:zip-0032"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0032"}," account, and can be used by wallets to derive encryption keys for local / off-chain metadata."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["A wallet's main data source is the Zcash chain: from this it can detect notes received by an account, determine whether those notes are spent, build witnesses for spending, recover on-chain memo data, and so on. However, wallets also generate significant quantities of off-chain metadata as they are used, such as:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["Local annotations about transactions in the wallet."]},{"tag":"li","children":["Mappings between Zcash addresses and user-meaningful recipient names."]},{"tag":"li","children":["The exchange rate from ZEC to another currency that was used to determine how much ZEC to send in a payment."]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["This metadata is valuable to users, and highly desirable to ensure to be backed up. If the user's device is wiped or lost and the user recovers their wallet from a backed-up mnemonic phrase, they will lose all of this metadata if it is not stored somewhere."]},{"tag":"p","children":["For other kinds of mobile device data, it is expected by users that their device's normal backup storage will have saved (most of) their data, such that access to e.g. the associated Apple or Google account will be sufficient for data recovery. However, metadata such as mappings between Zcash addresses and recipient names can be particularly sensitive, meaning that users may not want these to be backed up unencrypted in their device's normal backup storage. Similarly, the inability to alter on-chain data means that permanently storing metadata in transaction memo fields may also not be an option."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Additionally, it is currently the case that users only need to back up a single secret (a mnemonic seed phrase), once, in order to recover all information for accounts derived from that secret. If metadata were encrypted using independent key material, these keys would also need to be backed up, leading to fragility of wallet restoration."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Requirements"],"id":"requirements"},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["The user should not need to update their existing backups of secret material."]},{"tag":"li","children":["It should be possible to store metadata about accounts for which we don't control spend authority (i.e. imported UFVKs)."]},{"tag":"li","children":["The key tree must be future-extensible."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Metadata key tree"],"id":"metadatakeytree"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP registers the following ZIP 32 Registered Key Derivation ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"href":"#fn:zip-0032-rkd"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0032-rkd"}," tree:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖢"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗑"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗀"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["="]},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mtext","children":["“"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝙼"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚝"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚊"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚊"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝚝"]},{"tag":"mi",